---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site, demoHref } from '../data/site';
import '../styles/home-v2.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={site.wordmark}
  description="School administration for private schools in Telangana and Andhra Pradesh: admissions, attendance, assessments, report cards and a guardian portal in one connected record."
>
  <!-- GTM-WEBSITE-V2 P1: first-screen design pilot. Demo composition, not a product screenshot. -->
  <div class="home-v2">
    <section class="v2-hero" aria-labelledby="v2-hero-heading">
      <div class="wrap v2-hero-grid">
        <div class="v2-hero-copy">
          <span class="v2-label">For private schools in Telangana &amp; Andhra Pradesh</span>
          <h1 id="v2-hero-heading">A clearer way to <span>run your school.</span></h1>
          <p class="v2-hero-lead">
            From admission to published report cards, keep everyday school work connected.
            Administrators, teachers and guardians see information according to their roles.
          </p>
          <div class="v2-hero-actions">
            <a class="v2-btn v2-btn-primary" href={demoHref}>Request a demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="v2-btn v2-btn-secondary" href="/features/">Explore the features <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <p class="v2-hero-note">
            A dedicated installation, configured for each school's classes, terms and policies.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="v2-hero-art" aria-labelledby="v2-art-caption">
          <div class="v2-float v2-float-one" aria-hidden="true">
            <strong><span class="v2-float-dot"></span>Attendance</strong>
            <span>Class 8A register submitted</span>
          </div>
          <div class="v2-product-window" role="img"
            aria-label="Original illustrative school administration interface showing an overview, a reviewed admission, submitted attendance and report-card publication stages. Not a screenshot of the application.">
            <div class="v2-product-sidebar" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="v2-sidebar-brand"><i class="v2-sidebar-mark"></i>School ERP</div>
              <span class="v2-sidebar-link is-active">Overview</span>
              <span class="v2-sidebar-link">Students</span>
              <span class="v2-sidebar-link">Attendance</span>
              <span class="v2-sidebar-link">Assessments</span>
              <span class="v2-sidebar-link">Reports</span>
            </div>
            <div class="v2-ui-main" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="v2-ui-top">
                <div>
                  <div class="v2-ui-eyebrow">Fictional demo school</div>
                  <div class="v2-ui-title">School overview</div>
                </div>
                <span class="v2-ui-year">Academic year</span>
              </div>
              <div class="v2-ui-grid">
                <div class="v2-ui-tile">
                  <span>Admissions</span>
                  <strong>Application reviewed</strong>
                  <span class="v2-ui-pill">Decision recorded</span>
                </div>
                <div class="v2-ui-tile">
                  <span>Daily attendance</span>
                  <strong>Class 8A</strong>
                  <span class="v2-ui-pill">Register submitted</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="v2-ui-bottom">
                <div class="v2-ui-row"><span>Teacher marks entry</span><b class="v2-ui-state">Recorded</b></div>
                <div class="v2-ui-row"><span>School review</span><b class="v2-ui-state">Preview first</b></div>
                <div class="v2-ui-row"><span>Guardian report view</span><b class="v2-ui-state">After publication</b></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="v2-float v2-float-two" aria-hidden="true">
            <strong><span class="v2-float-dot"></span>Publication control</strong>
            <span>Results visible only after the school publishes</span>
          </div>
          <figcaption id="v2-art-caption" class="v2-art-caption">
            Original illustrative demo composition. Not an application screenshot.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="v2-proof-strip" aria-label="Core school workflow">
      <div class="wrap v2-proof-inner">
        <span class="v2-proof-lead">One connected school record</span>
        <span>Admissions</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <span>Daily work</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <span>Published results</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Why schools look for a system</span>
        <h2 id="problem-heading">When school work is spread across registers, files and spreadsheets</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          It becomes hard to see what is complete, what is missing and what is ready to share with families.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Admissions records, registers, marks and reports often sit in different places.</li>
        <li>Teachers need a clear view of the classes and work assigned to them.</li>
        <li>Management needs to review progress before results reach families.</li>
        <li>Guardians need secure access to information about their own children.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-white" aria-labelledby="journey-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">From admission to results</span>
        <h2 id="journey-heading">Follow each student through one record</h2>
        <p>
          The office decides admissions. Guardians see records only after the school grants access or publishes
          results.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps steps-3">
        <li>
          <h3>Register the applicant</h3>
          <p>The office records the application and the guardians linked to it.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Decide admission</h3>
          <p>Each application is explicitly accepted or rejected.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Enrol the student</h3>
          <p>Assign the academic year, class and section, with history kept.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Record school work</h3>
          <p>Attendance and marks follow the student through the year.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Review and publish</h3>
          <p>The office finalises assessments and releases report cards.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Family access</h3>
          <p>The guardian views the child’s released records.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="roles-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Built around roles</span>
        <h2 id="roles-heading">The right work for each person</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-label">Administrator</span>
          <h3>Coordinate school work</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Set up years, terms, classes, sections, subjects and the calendar</li>
            <li>Review applications, admit students and keep placement history</li>
            <li>Manage teaching assignments and check attendance and assessment progress</li>
            <li>Control report-card publication, notices and documents</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-label">Teacher</span>
          <h3>Focus on assigned classes</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>See the day’s work and configured timetable periods</li>
            <li>As class teacher, take attendance and submit the complete register</li>
            <li>Enter marks for assigned subjects</li>
            <li>Add class-teacher remarks where permitted</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-label">Guardian</span>
          <h3>See the right information</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Sign in to view children the school has approved access for</li>
            <li>Read submitted attendance and the monthly calendar</li>
            <li>Open published report cards and eligible PDF downloads</li>
            <li>Read notices meant for the child’s school, class or section</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band" aria-labelledby="publish-heading">
    <div class="wrap band-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Review before release</span>
        <h2 id="publish-heading">Marks stay private until the school publishes</h2>
        <p>
          Teachers enter results. The office finalises assessments, previews the report card and explicitly
          publishes it. Only then does it appear in the guardian portal. If a relevant correction is made later,
          the old publication is flagged for review.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/features/#daily-work">Read about assessments and report cards</a></p>
      </div>
      <figure class="publish-figure">
        <ol class="publish-flow" aria-label="Report card publication stages (illustration)">
          <li>Teacher enters marks and remarks <span class="state">Not visible</span></li>
          <li>Office finalises the assessment <span class="state">Not visible</span></li>
          <li>Office previews the report card <span class="state">Not visible</span></li>
          <li>Office publishes it <span class="state state-live">Visible to guardian</span></li>
        </ol>
        <figcaption>Illustration of the stages, not a product screenshot.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="fit-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">How it works for a school</span>
        <h2 id="fit-heading">Practical from the first term</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Your own installation</h3>
          <p>
            Each school has its own installation, configured with its academic year, terms, classes, subjects,
            weekly pattern, holidays and grading scales.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Start from your spreadsheets</h3>
          <p>
            Import students, guardians and class placements from the Excel template. Every row is checked, and
            problems are shown before anything is saved.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Works in the browser</h3>
          <p>
            Use it on office computers and phones. On supported phones it can be added to the home screen. It
            needs an internet connection; there is no offline mode.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Staff-assisted WhatsApp messages</h3>
          <p>
            WhatsApp Assist prepares messages, such as same-day absence alerts, for guardians who have consented.
            Staff send each one from WhatsApp; nothing is sent automatically.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-lg">
        <a href="/faq/#product-boundaries">See what the current product does not include</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
